.If someone is round and big, then they like the lion.\n17.If someone is green, then they visit the tiger.\n18.If someone eats the tiger and they are not nice, then the tiger likes the lion.\nIf the lion doesn\'t like the tiger and someone eats the squirrel, then the tiger dislikes the lion.\nFrom the given information, it is clear that the lion dislikes the squirrel. However, we must verify if this dislike is influenced by the elephant\'s feelings towards the lion. Let\'s examine the pertinent details:\n- The squirrel avoids both the mouse and the tiger.\n- The squirrel dislikes the lion.\n- The lion feeds the mouse.\n- The lion is blue.\n- The mouse is cruel.\n- The tiger is cruel and mean.\n- The mouse turns blue if someone avoids the mouse and encounters the tiger.\n- The lion avoids the tiger if it is mean.\n- The mouse grows small if it turns blue.\n- The lion likes the tiger if it is mean.\nBased on this data, we can infer that the mouse is not blue because the lion feeds the mouse and the lion avoids the tiger. Consequently, the mouse is not blue, indicating the mouse is small and dislikes the lion. Since the squirrel dislikes the lion and the squirrel avoids the mouse, it is sensible to presume that the mouse dislikes the lion as well.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
