ie is not smart."Since Charlie is indeed big and young, this statement tells us that Charlie is not smart.\nNow, let\'s consider the statement "If Fiona is big and Fiona is not white then Fiona is blue."This statement doesn\'t directly affect Charlie\'s color, as it only applies to Fiona.\nFinally, let\'s look at the statement "If Charlie is big and Charlie is young then Charlie is not smart."Since Charlie is big and young, this statement confirms that Charlie is not smart.\nSince Charlie is not smart and all blue things are young, and young, white things are round, we can conclude that Charlie cannot be white.If Charlie were white, he would have to be young and round, which would contradict the fact that he is not smart\n. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
