 information about the color of the mouse and whether it is young, we can definitively conclude whether the mouse is young or not young.\n8.The information provided is sufficient to determine the age of the mouse.\nTherefore, based on the given context, we can determine that the mouse is young. The information is sufficient to make a definitive conclusion.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
