und.\n16.If something is round and it sees the cow, then the cow sees the rabbit.\n17.If something is big, then it visits the cow.\n18.If something sees the rabbit, then the rabbit visits the bald eagle.\n19.If something is blue, then it likes the rabbit.\n20.If something likes the cow and the cow is young, then it is blue.\nFrom the context, we can see that:.\n- The bald eagle likes the cow (point 1).\n- The cow likes the bald eagle (point 2).\n- The rabbit sees the bald eagle (point 3).\n- The rabbit likes the bald eagle (point 4).\n- The cow sees the rabbit (point 5).\nFrom the above analysis, we can see that the bald eagle dislikes the rabbit (point 4).. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
