messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is nice. Anne is young. Dave is cold. Dave is smart. Dave is white. Fiona is nice. Fiona is not red. Fiona is young. Gary is cold. Gary is red. If someone is smart then they are green. If someone is green then they are nice. Nice people are young. If someone is white then they are young. If someone is cold then they are white. If someone is green and smart then they are white. All young, red people are smart. If Fiona is red then Fiona is green. If Anne is smart then Anne is not green.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is not smart.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Gary is not smart" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context, we need to carefully analyze the information provided and apply logical reasoning step by step.Let\'s break down the context and question:.\n\n1.**Anne is nice.Anne is young.**.\n2.**Dave is cold.Dave is smart.Dave is white.**.\n3.**Fiona is nice.Fiona is not red.Fiona is young.**.\n4.**Gary is cold.Gary is red.**.\n5.**If someone is smart then they are green.**.\n6.**If someone is green then they are nice.**.\n7.**Nice people are young.**.\n8.**If someone is white then they are young.**.\n9.**If someone is cold then they are white.**.\n10.**If someone is green and smart then they are white.**.\n11.**All young, red people are smart.**.\n12.**If Fiona is red then Fiona is green.**.\n13.**If Anne is smart then Anne is not green.**.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Gary is not smart" using the given information:.\n\n- From the context, we know that Gary is cold and red.\n- According to point 9, if someone is white, they are young.Since Gary is not red, we don\'t need to check if Gary is white.\n- From point 8, if someone is not green and not smart, they are not white.Since Gary is smart (we need to determine this), we need to check this condition directly.\n- From point 11, if Fiona is not red, then Fiona is not green.However, Fiona is red, so this condition applies to Gary.\n- From point 10, if someone is not green and not smart, they are not white.Since Gary is smart, this condition applies to Gary.\n- From point 7, nice people are not young.Since Gary is mentioned as nice, we can directly conclude he is not nice.\n- From point 6, if someone is not green, they are not nice.Since Gary is green, we can directly conclude he is not nice.\n- From point 5, Dave is not smart.However, Dave is Gary, so Dave\'s smartness affects Gary\'s status.\n\nGiven the information, we need to determine if Gary is not smart or not:.\n- Gary is not cold and not red.\n- If Gary were not smart, he would not be green (from point 9).\n- If Gary were not green, he would not be nice (from point 6).\n- If Gary were not nice, he would not be young (from point 7).\n\nSince Gary is not red, he can be white (from point 8).Therefore, Gary can be green (from point 9), and he can be nice (from point 6).Since Gary is nice, he can be young (from point 7).\n\nThus, Gary can be smart because if he were not, he would not have to be green, which aligns with the fact that he is red\n. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
