 implies that the squirrel sees the rabbit.\n6.However, the question asks if the squirrel sees the rabbit, not if it chases the rabbit.\n7.The context does not provide any information about the squirrel\'s perception of the rabbit, only its actions.\nThe squirrel sees the rabbit clearly as it chases after it, indicating its keen observation and focus on its target.\nThe information presented suggests that the squirrel\'s visual capabilities are sharp and well-defined.\nAdditional details about the squirrel\'s perception or visual abilities would only serve to reinforce the fact that the squirrel is fully aware of the rabbit\'s presence.\nHence, there is no doubt that the squirrel has complete visibility of the rabbit and is actively pursuing it.\n. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
