heless, this clearly gives direct information about the mouse seeing the lion.\n6.We also have no information about the lion ignoring the dog, the lion ignoring the mouse, and the lion missing the dog.But all of these statements directly relate to the mouse seeing the lion.\n7.The context does provide information about the mouse seeing the lion or not.\n8.Therefore, based on the given information, we can confidently determine that the mouse sees the lion.\n9\n. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
