he squirrel is indeed blue.\n\n3.**Logical Deductions:**.\n   - Given the context, it is evident that the squirrel is not green and smooth.\n   - Because the squirrel is smooth, it is small (as stated in the information that smooth things are small).\n   - The assertion "If something is blue then it avoids the lion" directly relates to the squirrel since the squirrel is blue.\n   - The assertion "If something avoids the lion and it catches the squirrel then the squirrel sees the tiger" applies to the squirrel because the squirrel avoids the lion and catches it.\n   - The assertion "If the squirrel catches the lion and the squirrel is green then the lion sees the tiger" applies to the squirrel because the squirrel catches the lion.\n   - The assertion "If something sees the tiger then it is blue" applies to the squirrel because the squirrel sees the tiger.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**\n. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
