If the lion eats the squirrel and the lion sees the cat then the lion is young.**.\n   - This rule does not directly apply to the bald eagle.\n\n5.**If something is cold then it chases the cat.**.\n   - This rule does not directly apply to the bald eagle.\n\n6.**If the squirrel eats the bald eagle and the bald eagle is cold then the bald eagle is round.**.\n   - This rule directly relates to the bald eagle\'s roundness.However, it requires two conditions to be true:.\n     a.The squirrel eats the bald eagle.\n     b.The bald eagle is cold.\n\nThe bald eagle is not round based on the given information that it is cold and the squirrel eats it.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
