\n\nNow, let's analyze the statement \"The bear visits the rabbit\":\n- We know the rabbit visits the bear (from point 8).\n- However, the context does not provide any information about the bear visiting the rabbit.\n\nGiven that we do not have any information about the bear visiting the rabbit, we cannot determine whether this statement is true or false. Therefore, the statement is unknown based on the provided information.\n\n<answer>\nC) Unknown\n</answer>",
