n people are young.Since Charlie is not green and white, this statement contradicts our previous conclusion.\n10.The context implies that Dave is not young.However, this information alone doesn\'t tell us if Dave is kind or not.\n11.The context implies that not all rough, kind people are big.However, this information doesn\'t directly relate to Dave\'s kindliness or roughness.\n12.The context implies that not all big, rough people are furry.However, this information doesn\'t directly relate to Dave\'s kindliness or roughness.\n13.The context implies that unkind people are not green.However, this information doesn\'t directly relate to Dave\'s kindliness.\nBased on this analysis, we can see that the context provides conflicting information about Charlie\'s kindliness, greenness, and roughness, and it doesn\'t give us any direct information about Dave\'s kindliness.The only information we have about Dave is that he is not young, but this doesn\'t necessarily mean he is kind\n. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
