lor.\n10.The statement "Harry is not green and Harry is not young" is given, so we can use it to determine Harry\'s color.\n11.The statement "Green people are not white" is directly relevant to Bob, as it only applies to green people in general.\n12.The statement "All young people are not cold" is directly relevant to Bob, as it only applies to young people in general.\n13.The statement "If someone is not smart then they are not young" is directly relevant to Bob, as it only applies to smart people in general.\n14.The statement "If someone is not furry then they are not green" is directly relevant to Bob, as it only applies to furry people in general.\n15.The statement "If someone is not green and cold then they are not white" is directly relevant to Bob, as it only applies to green and cold people in general.\nGiven this analysis, we can conclude that there is direct information provided about Bob\'s color. The context only tells us that Bob is not cold, and while we know that all cold people are not furry, we can determine if Bob is green or not.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
