messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is furry. Anne is nice. Anne is rough. Anne is white. Erin is furry. Erin is rough. Erin is white. Fiona is big. Fiona is nice. Fiona is round. Harry is nice. Harry is rough. All furry things are white. If Harry is red then Harry is round. All round, red things are furry. If Harry is rough then Harry is round. Nice, red things are big. Round, red things are white. All nice, white things are red. If something is round then it is furry.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Erin is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Erin is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context, I need to carefully analyze the information provided step by step.\nFirst, let\'s summarize the key information:.\n1.Anne is furry, nice, rough, and white.\n2.Erin is furry, rough, and white.\n3.Fiona is big, nice, and round.\n4.Harry is nice, rough, and round.\n5.All furry things are white.\n6.If Harry is red then Harry is round.\n7.All round, red things are furry.\n8.If Harry is rough then Harry is round.\n9.Nice, red things are big.\n10.Round, red things are white.\n11.All nice, white things are red.\n12.If something is round then it is furry.\nNow, let\'s focus on Erin:.Erin is not furry and smooth. \nWe know that all furry things are not white, so Erin is not white. \nWe also know that all round, red things are not furry, and if Harry is not rough then Harry is not round. Since Harry is not rough, Harry is not round. Therefore, Harry is not furry. \nSince Erin is not rough and all rough things are not white, Erin is not white. \nWe have some information about Erin\'s size. \nThe statement "Nice, red things are big" applies to Erin because she is nice. \nThe statement "Round, red things are white" applies to Erin because she is round. \nThe statement "All nice, white things are red" applies to Erin because she is nice. \nThe statement "If something is round then it is furry" applies to Erin because she is round. \nGiven this analysis, we can conclude that there is information provided that directly or indirectly confirms or denies Erin\'s size.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
